Michael Lehotay wrote:
> The limit is 640000 points, which is what you would get if you reached
> experience level 15 just by killing monsters. I think somebody said in
> the scoring system thread that reaching level 15 without magic is
> pretty much impossible, and that's how I picked this number. Feedback
> would be very much appreciated.

I think stop getting score for kills after a certain experience level is a 
bad idea. But getting too much score from kills is also not good. Well, I 
though some about it and came up with this:

If i'm not mistaken the current formula is something like this

S0 = C*X + R

where S0 is the score, C is a constant (4?), X is experience points and R is 
the rest of the score (from gems and such).
Michael's proposal whould be

S1 = min(C*X, M) + R

where M is some maximum score (640000).
Now, I though, isn't there a function that is close to S0 for small X and 
smothly flattens to a horizontal asymptote for large X. I found

S3 = M*(1 - 1/A * LN(1 + EXP(A * (1 - C/M * X)))) + R

where M is the maximum score, A is a constant which controlls the tightness 
of the transition between the asymptotes. For larger A the graph of S3 looks 
more like that of S2.
For example: C = 4, M = 5000000, A = 4 makes the value of the function be 
within 6% of the original for X = 160000 (level 15, right?).
These values were almost randomly choosen for testing, they will need to be 
tweeked for this to be a good scoring function.

Ok, that was very mathematical, in plain english it means that up until 
about level 15 you get almost the same score as with the current version. 
But when you have much xp the amount of score per new xp goes down until, 
when you have infinite score, the gain becomes zero. At that point you have 
reached the maximum score.

That was just my 2, rather advanced, cents. I'm going back to lurking now...

